UPDATE companies SET description='Soft Goods operates a garment factory in Detroit, Michigan, where it produces a range of cotton knitwear including t‑shirts, sweatshirts, sweatpants, robes, and headwear. The company owns and runs its production facility in the city, cutting and sewing each piece by hand using natural fibers.

The product line centers on heavyweight cotton basics — classic crewneck tees, double‑front sweatpants, jersey pants, French terry hooded robes, and thermal layers. All garments are assembled in the Detroit shop in small batches; nothing is mass‑produced, and every item passes through the hands of the makers. The factory handles cutting, sewing, and finishing for the brand’s own collections.

Soft Goods sells its own labeled apparel directly to consumers through its e‑commerce site, serving customers who value domestically made, natural‑fiber clothing. The brand positions its goods as everyday wear shaped by “real work” and Detroit workshop values, appealing to buyers seeking durable, honestly constructed basics.

The company emphasizes that its differentiation lies in full vertical control — owning the factory, using only natural fibers, and rejecting mass‑production methods. It frames its approach as a return to “grit and persistent craftsmanship,” where each garment is a labor of love rather than a commodity output.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut and sew", "Garment assembly", "Hand sewing", "Small batch production"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Knitwear", "Clothing"], "materials": ["Cotton", "French terry", "Fleece", "Natural fibers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Owned and operated cut\u2011and\u2011sew factory in Detroit", "Garments handcrafted from natural fibers only", "Small\u2011batch production; no mass\u2011manufacturing", "Free domestic shipping on orders over $200"], "facts_used": ["Detroit, Michigan headquarters -> db", "Owns and operates factory in Detroit -> /", "Produces cotton knitwear (t\u2011shirts, sweatshirts, sweatpants, robes, headwear) -> /", "Garments cut and sewn by hand using natural fibers -> /", "Small\u2011batch, non\u2011mass\u2011production approach -> /", "Direct\u2011to\u2011consumer sales via website -> /", "Free domestic shipping on orders over $200 -> /", "Materials: cotton, French terry, fleece -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We own and operate our factory in Detroit and make garments the way they used to be made. By hand and with natural fibers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='soft-goods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Softline Brand Partners was founded in March 2014 in Minneapolis, Minnesota, born from a passion for creating high-quality soft goods. The company operates as a full-service contract manufacturer with a vertically integrated model that spans design, sourcing, and production.

The firm produces a range of soft goods including small leather goods, bags, home goods, watch straps, patches and labels, and strap goods. It runs cut-and-sew operations in domestic factories across the Midwest and East Coast as well as overseas facilities in China, Vietnam, India, Mexico, Europe, and Central America. The company notes it has scaled clients from 100-unit runs to orders of millions of units, with one partner growing from 5,000 monthly units to over 1,000,000 units in under 18 months.

Named partners include Love Your Melon, Bespoke Post, Allen Edmonds, Fastanal, Timex, Room & Board, Leesa Sleep, and Acco.

