UPDATE companies SET description='Solid State Devices, Inc. (SSDI) has operated from La Mirada, California since its founding in 1967. The company began as a supplier of hermetic semiconductor devices for critical aerospace and defense applications and has remained at that location for over five decades.

SSDI designs and manufactures high-power and high-voltage semiconductor components, including rectifiers, IGBTs, thyristors, power modules, hybrids, and assemblies. Its La Mirada facility houses wafer fabrication, assembly, and test operations, with capabilities spanning die attach, wire bonding, hermetic sealing, and a full suite of environmental and reliability screening per MIL-PRF-19500, MIL-STD-883, and related standards. The company also offers custom packaging, reverse engineering, and end-of-life solutions.

The primary customers are aerospace and defense programs, including U.S. military and space agencies. SSDI''s products are qualified to JANS, the highest reliability level under MIL-PRF-19500, and the company works directly with procurement groups and design engineers on source-controlled drawings for missiles, satellites, and avionics.

SSDI emphasizes its combined 700-plus years of engineering experience drawn from alumni of firms such as Microsemi, International Rectifier, and Motorola. It maintains in-house wafer fabrication and assembly, a strong anti-counterfeit program, material lot traceability, and a willingness to accept small-quantity orders — factors the company cites as differentiators in a market often focused on high-volume production.', certifications=ARRAY['JANS','ISO 9001','AS9100']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High-voltage rectifier manufacturing", "IGBT manufacturing", "Thyristor/SCR manufacturing", "Power module and hybrid assembly", "Wafer fabrication (diffusion, metallization, dicing)", "Die attach and wire bonding", "Hermetic sealing (cap weld, seam seal, glass encapsulation)", "Environmental testing (thermal shock, temperature cycling, humidity, salt spray, vibration, shock, acceleration)", "Reliability screening (burn-in, power cycling, HTRB, PIND, real-time X-ray)", "Electrical testing per MIL-PRF-19500, MIL-STD-883, MIL-STD-750, MIL-STD-202, ESA SCC-5000, MIL-M-38510, MIL-PRF-38534", "Custom packaging and reverse engineering", "End-of-life / DMS solutions"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)"], "equipment": ["Belt Furnaces", "Die Attach Stations", "Hot Gas Bonder", "Die Probes", "Passivation equipment", "Wire Bonders", "Cap Welders", "Seam Sealers", "DAP Assembly equipment", "Resistance Welder", "Vapor Phase system", "Encapsulation equipment", "DAP Sealer", "Machine Shop / CNC Machine", "Wet Chemistry Bench (Clean)", "High Temperature Diffusion Furnaces", "Varian Evaporator (Lifetime Control / Metallization)", "Die Saw / Sandblast Dicer (Wafer Dicing)", "Glass Encapsulation equipment", "Die Etch equipment", "ATE \u2013 TESEC 3000 V, 200 A", "Fine Leak Testing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["JANS-certified wafer fabrication and assembly facilit