UPDATE companies SET description='Solid State Logic is headquartered in New York, New York, while its original manufacturing and research base remains at Begbroke Manor in Oxfordshire, UK. The company was founded in 1969 by Colin Sanders CBE, who initially developed switching systems for pipe organs before establishing Acorn Studios in the village of Stonesfield. There he built the first SSL consoles, to the SL 4000 B Series in 1976 and the breakthrough SL 4000 E Series in 1979 that transformed professional recording.

Today SSL designs and manufactures a wide range of audio hardware and software: large-format analogue and digital consoles for music, broadcast, and live sound; desktop audio interfaces; DAW controllers; 19-inch rackmount processors; 500-series modules; and an extensive library of native plug-ins. Production occurs at the 4,000-square-meter facility opened at Begbroke Manor in 1988, though current headcount and annual volumes are not disclosed.

The company serves music production studios, broadcast facilities, live-sound rental companies, post-production houses, educational institutions, installed-sound venues, touring acts, and podcast/webcast creators.

SSL differentiates itself through proprietary technologies such as SuperAnalogue™ circuitry, console-wide Instant Recall, motorised fader automation (Ultimation), and native ST 2110 IP workflows with NMOS discovery. The founder’s original drive to improve organ switching evolved into a philosophy of continuous innovation in audio signal processing and workflow integration.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Analogue console design and manufacturing", "Digital console design and manufacturing", "Audio interface design and manufacturing", "DAW controller design and manufacturing", "Analogue outboard processor design and manufacturing", "500-series module design and manufacturing", "Audio plug-in software development", "Broadcast audio production system design", "Live sound console design", "ST 2110 IP audio routing and processing", "Virtualised audio processing deployment", "Cloud-based audio production", "SSL Certified Training"], "industries": ["Music production", "Live sound", "Broadcast", "Post production", "Education", "Installed sound", "Touring & events", "Podcast & webcast", "OB & sports production"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SL 4000 E Series", "SL 9000 J Series", "System T (S500, S500m, S400, S300)", "Odyssey", "Oracle", "ORIGIN Series", "AWS \u03b4elta", "Duality Fuse", "L650", "L550 Plus", "SSL 12", "SSL 18", "UF8", "TE2 Tempest Engine", "TE1 Tempest Engine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SuperAnalogue\u2122 circuitry for high bandwidth and low distortion", "Console-wide Instant Recall across all parameters", "Motorised fader automation (Ultimation) since the 1990s", "Native ST 2110 IP audio routing with NMOS IS-04/IS-05", "Virtualised on-prem and cloud production deployment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 by Colin Sanders CBE -> /about", "First products: switching systems for pipe organs -> /about", "Acorn Studios in Stonesfield, Oxfordshire -> /about", "SL 4000 B Series 1976, SL 4000 E Series 1979 -> /about", "Moved HQ to Begbroke Manor 1986, 4,000m2 facility opened 1988 -> /about", "SuperAnalogue\u2122 design introduced in SL 9000 J Series -> /about", "Ultimation motorised fader automation 1990s -> /about", "C100 On-Air console 2003, C200, C300, C100 HDS, C10 HD -> /about", "AWS 2004, Duality 2006 hybrid consoles -> /about", "Headquarters New York, New York per database -> db", "Product lines: Odyssey, Oracle, ORIGIN, AWS \u03b4elta, Duality Fuse, System T, L650, SSL 12, SSL 18, UF8, TE2/TE1 -> /", "Industries served: music production, live sound, broadcast, post production, education, installed sound, touring, podcast, OB sports -> /", "ST 2110 native IP workflows with NMOS -> /", "Virtualised on-prem and cloud production -> /", "SSL Certified Training Partner Directory -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "world''s leading manufacturer of creative tools for music, live sound and broadcast", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/solid-state-logic/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solid-state-logic' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solr Standard is based in Warminster, Pennsylvania. The company was founded with the goal of delivering high-quality solar solutions without the confusion, pressure, or shortcuts often associated with the industry, though a specific founding year and founder names are not disclosed.

The firm provides solar system design, project planning, and coordination services for residential, commercial, and energy storage projects. It works with a network of qualified installation partners to execute installations and also offers roofing services through Roofing Standard. The company emphasizes a thoughtful evaluation of each property, energy usage, and future goals to develop properly sized, efficient systems using premium panels, carefully selected inverters, and battery systems chosen for reliability.

Solr Standard serves homeowners, property managers, and business owners across Pennsylvania and New Jersey. Its project portfolio ranges from residential rooftop systems to commercial-scale solar arrays and battery backup installations, all supported by deep local knowledge of utility incentives, permitting requirements, and regional weather conditions.

