UPDATE companies SET description='Sonoran Stitch Factory operates from Tucson, Arizona. The company was founded by Erica Yngve, a serial entrepreneur who also owns three brands manufactured at the facility: Bralessly, Postcraft Products, and Palmfree Sunwear. Yngve’s background includes manufacturing operations, an import partnership, and an MBA in operations management from DePaul University.

The factory specializes in sewn goods production with a focus on knit apparel and small to medium batch runs. Its services span production flow management, inventory control, fulfillment, shipping, and quality assurance. The team reports 27-plus client brands and more than 160,000 units sewn to date, supported by a skilled operator base and a production manager with deep textile experience.

Customers range from emerging apparel labels to established industrial suppliers. Postcraft Products, a 90-year-old company, relies on the factory for industrial sewn goods used in housing, healthcare, hospitality, and cruise ships. Palmfree Sunwear produces sun-protective gloves for golf, tennis, pickleball, and gardening.

The company’s stated mission centers on three pillars: building a sustainable, profitable, human-centered production model; delivering high-quality domestic manufacturing; and creating pathways into manufacturing careers through apprenticeships and student training (209 students trained, two apprentices sponsored). Yngve frames the operation as a partnership that brings practical, owner-level insight to every client project.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sewn goods production", "Knit apparel manufacturing", "Small to medium batch production", "Production flow management", "Inventory management", "Fulfillment and shipping", "Quality control", "Production scaling support", "Apprenticeship training"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Fashion", "Industrial sewn products", "Healthcare", "Hospitality", "Cruise ships", "Outdoor recreation", "Sun protective apparel"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small to medium batch production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Partnership-based production model with transparency and clarity", "In-house expertise from founder\u2019s own brands manufactured on-site", "Small to medium batch sewn goods specialization", "Workforce development via apprenticeships and student training (209 trained, 2 sponsored)", "Domestic production in Tucson, Arizona"], "facts_used": ["Location: Tucson, Arizona -> db", "Founder: Erica Yngve, President -> /about-us", "Mission: sustainability, quality, community -> /", "Metrics: 27+ clients, 160,000+ products sewn, 209 students trained, 2 apprentices sponsored -> /", "Capabilities: sewn goods, knit apparel, small to medium batch, production flow, inventory, fulfillment, shipping, quality control -> /about-us", "Industries: apparel, industrial sewn products for housing, healthcare, hospitality, cruise ships, outdoor recreation, sun protective wear -> /about-us", "Team: Erica Yngve (President), Maggie Marquez (Production Manager) -> /about-us", "Own brands: Bralessly, Postcraft Products, Palmfree Sunwear -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We provide a professional, reliable production partner who can take ownership of manufacturing so you can stay focused on building your business.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sonoran-stitch-factory' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='What began as a personal project turned into a side business helping friends add solar to their own rigs, and the operation was formalized under the SotaSolar.com domain in 2019. By 2020 the founders committed to solar full time, and in winter 2023 they established a permanent shop in Nowthen to house the growing team.

The business designs, sells, and installs custom off-grid and RV solar systems built around Victron Energy inverters, chargers, and monitoring gear, along with lithium iron phosphate (LiFePO4) batteries. Services include system estimation, consultation, and full installation for travel trailers, fifth wheels, Class A motorhomes, Airstreams, and, as of 2026, marine vessels. The shop also stocks Victron MultiPlus and Quattro inverter/chargers, Cerbo GX monitors, and battery balancers, and provides ongoing service and support for the systems it commissions.

Customers range from weekend campers to full-time live-aboards who need reliable power without generator noise or campground hookups. Each build follows a stated philosophy: safe, serviceable, easy to use, and clean enough to be proud of.

The founders say the company was started to give people who leave the grid behind a knowledgeable local partner—expert guidance before the sale, proper integration of panels, batteries, and inverters, and responsive support afterward. That dealer-installer model, combined with a focus on clean, serviceable workmanship, is presented as the core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design", "Solar system installation", "Off-grid solar system design", "RV solar system installation", "Marine solar & battery system installation", "System estimation & consultation", "Victron Energy product sales & configuration", "Lithium LiFePO4 battery sales & installation", "Cerbo GX monitoring system setup", "Battery balancing & management", "Electrical system integration", "Custom battery bank assembly"], "industries": ["Recreational vehicles (RV)", "Marine", "Off-grid residential", "Golf cart / light electric vehicle"], "materials": ["Lithium iron phosphate (LiFePO4) batteries", "Solar panels", "Victron Energy components", "Electrical wiring and components"], "equipment": ["Victron Energy MultiPlus inverter/charger", "Victron Energy Quattro inverter/charger", "Victron Energy Cerbo GX monitoring system", "Victron Energy Battery Balancer", "Lithium LiFePO4 battery banks"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"Safe. Serviceable. Easy to use. And clean enough to be proud of.\" build philosophy", "Local Victron Energy dealer providing expert pre-sale guidance and post-sale support", "Custom system design tailored to each RV''s specific space and power needs", "Full integration of panels, batteries, inverters, and monitoring for maximum performance", "Ongoing service and support for the life of the system"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2017 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Nowthen, Minnesota -> db, /about-us", "Victron Energy dealer & installer -> /", "Lithium LiFePO4 battery sales & installation -> /", "RV types served: travel trailers, 5th wheels, Class As, Airstreams -> /", "Marine services launched 2026 -> /about-us", "Shop established in Nowthen winter 2023 -> /about-us", "Build philosophy: safe, serviceable, easy to use, clean -> /", "Services: design, estimation, consultation, installation -> /", "Victron MultiPlus, Quattro, Cerbo GX, Battery Balancer equipment -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design, sell and install Offgrid & RV solar systems around your needs and budget.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sota-rv-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Souhrada Manufacturing Inc. operates from Tyndall, South Dakota, as a family-owned industrial sewing company. The business has been producing custom sewn products for more than 26 years, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. No founders are named in the company''s public materials.

The company specializes in interior trim components for the heavy-truck market, including vinyl drapes, window curtains, mesh cabinet net assemblies, and custom straps. Beyond truck interiors, it produces soft-sided luggage, graduation gowns, pouches, industrial covers, heavy-duty nylon straps for agriculture, and fly-rod cases. Its facility houses more than a dozen industrial sewing machines (Brother, Juki, Mitsubishi) capable of single-needle, double-needle, zigzag, and four-thread serging, plus programmable bar-tack machines, a die-cutting press with a 60-by-17-inch bed, automated hot/cold strip cutters, a 60-foot spreading table, and an Eastman Brute vertical knife cutter that handles material up to 5.5 inches thick. Services extend to screen printing, embroidery, tensile testing, FMVSS 302 flammability testing, warehousing, and just-in-time distribution.

The company emphasizes design collaboration, prototyping, material sourcing, and full order fulfillment from a single site.

